Author: Aditi Vaidya [aut, cre], Anirudh Narayanan [aut], Anirudh Prasanna [aut], Arjun Arunachalam [aut], Deenabandhan N [aut], Mohit Rathi [aut]
Maintainer: Aditi Vaidya <aditiv2004@googlemail.com>
Description:
    Provides methods for efficient subdata selection for large-scale and high-dimensional regression problems. 
    The package implements Information-Based Optimal Subdata Selection (IBOSS) by Wang, Yang, and Stufken (2019) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2017.1408468>, 
    Generalized IBOSS (GenIBOSS) for non-linear models by Yu, Liu, and Wang (2023) <doi:10.1007/s00362-023-01430-3>, 
    Combining Lasso and Subdata Selection (CLASS) by Singh and Stufken (2023) <doi:10.51387/23-NEJSDS36>, 
    and Subsampled Randomized Hadamard Transform (SRHT) by Tropp et al. (2017) <doi:10.1137/17M1111590>. 
    CLASS identifies active variables through repeated LASSO fits on smaller data subsets and subsequently 
    uses IBOSS to select an informative subset of observations for regression. The package also implements 
    HT-CLASS, which applies a Hadamard transform before the row-sampling step to improve the identification 
    of active variables whose signals are concentrated in a small subset of observations.
